dth=\"277\" height=\"216\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc9d677b-3d60-43d2-943f-791c9dd6f2b6\" />\n<img width=\"250\" height=\"206\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6972ce70-cc7e-4b25-8402-898e9394e9f3\" />\n<img width=\"209\" height=\"163\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/139ba7df-32cf-472d-8173-e4898b831787\" />\n\nThe last image shows how it should look overall.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe project is quite complex, and it's difficult to reproduce everything as is, but I'd like to understand why there were no issues before Godot v4.7-dev4.\n\nAnd so, on the screen, there are polygon quadrants (2D), where, through online interaction (like an eraser), polygons are cut and glued together in a way that creates the feeling of drawing, while maintaining polygonality and full physical interaction (CollisionPolygon2D). In other words, the end result is a freehand drawing by the user, but in reality, seamlessly generated Polygon2D.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIt's possible this is some new parameter in camera2d behavior that crops some part by default. But it's unlikely.","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_ur